# armour/<body>/skirt_strips: STRIPS, five hanging strips 2 px wide with dark 1 px gaps from a seam under
# the fauld to mid-thigh (pteruges): the only vertical pattern of the kit, read at 1x as a striped fringe;
# a notched hem (the 1st, 3rd and 5th strips a row shorter), splayed a pixel in the run.
# Generated from the FORGE-LIMBS skirt templates (gen_skirts2.py, skirts_def.py; iteration 2: the D view serves U, `tags anyfacing`); Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (FORGE-LIMBS envelope r1) T5-T6 skirt flare (STYLE_P2 29.3): `armour.t5` views facing D/U, 1 px more past the hips on the lower half; flared copies of the replace views go before them. Generated by FORGE-LIMBS flare.py.
use person
body man
role overlay skirt.strips
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
tags anyfacing
z 10

# (FORGE-LIMBS envelope r2 breeze) the T5-T6 strips flare on their last three rows in the breeze (was one; C13: a masterwork strip skirt read still). breeze2.py
